{"type":"assistant","uuid":"f0be122e-a8a7-4ed3-af67-2f47912f9141","session_id":"9e1db7f8-0f8b-4b2f-bfcf-ad6e280193c8","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"f0be122e-a8a7-4ed3-af67-2f47912f9141","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe fix is verified. Here's the final summary:\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n**File:** `app/src/main/java/org/sufficientlysecure/htmltextview/LocalLinkMovementMethod.java`\n\n**Problem:** When a user long-presses a URL in a comment, the context menu appears (from the `OnLongClickListener` on `commentBody` in `CommentsRecyclerViewAdapter`), but the `LocalLinkMovementMethod.onTouchEvent()` also triggers the link click on `ACTION_UP` — opening the URL immediately.\n\n**Root cause:** `LocalLinkMovementMethod.onTouchEvent()` calls `link[0].onClick(widget)` synchronously on `ACTION_UP` without checking whether a long-press was intended.\n\n**Fix:** Added `ViewConfiguration` import and wrapped the `ACTION_UP` click dispatch with a `hasOnLongClickListeners()` guard. When a long-press listener is registered, the link click is deferred by `getLongPressTimeout()` (~400ms) via `postDelayed()`. This gives the long-press handler time to fire first, preventing the unwanted URL open.\n\n**Lines changed:**\n- Added import: `import android.view.ViewConfiguration;`\n- Lines 66–82: `ACTION_UP` handler now checks `widget.hasOnLongClickListeners()` — if true, defers `onClick()` with `postDelayed(getLongPressTimeout())`; if false, calls `onClick()` immediately (original behavior)."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":71827,"output_tokens":324,"cache_read_input_tokens":71264,"total_tokens":72151}}}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","uuid":"e8440c91-6950-4613-bfd6-9ad193641947","session_id":"9e1db7f8-0f8b-4b2f-bfcf-ad6e280193c8","is_error":false,"duration_ms":212941,"duration_api_ms":174358,"num_turns":51,"result":"\n\nThe fix is verified. Here's the final summary:\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n**File:** `app/src/main/java/org/sufficientlysecure/htmltextview/LocalLinkMovementMethod.java`\n\n**Problem:** When a user long-presses a URL in a comment, the context menu appears (from the `OnLongClickListener` on `commentBody` in `CommentsRecyclerViewAdapter`), but the `LocalLinkMovementMethod.onTouchEvent()` also triggers the link click on `ACTION_UP` — opening the URL immediately.\n\n**Root cause:** `LocalLinkMovementMethod.onTouchEvent()` calls `link[0].onClick(widget)` synchronously on `ACTION_UP` without checking whether a long-press was intended.\n\n**Fix:** Added `ViewConfiguration` import and wrapped the `ACTION_UP` click dispatch with a `hasOnLongClickListeners()` guard. When a long-press listener is registered, the link click is deferred by `getLongPressTimeout()` (~400ms) via `postDelayed()`. This gives the long-press handler time to fire first, preventing the unwanted URL open.\n\n**Lines changed:**\n- Added import: `import android.view.ViewConfiguration;`\n- Lines 66–82: `ACTION_UP` handler now checks `widget.hasOnLongClickListeners()` — if true, defers `onClick()` with `postDelayed(getLongPressTimeout())`; if false, calls `onClick()` immediately (original behavior).","usage":{"input_tokens":3533632,"output_tokens":26660,"cache_read_input_tokens":3095792,"total_tokens":3560292},"permission_denials":[]}
